    "summary_one_sentence": "Polar-opposite best friends Poppy and Alex attempt to repair their fractured relationship and confront their long-suppressed romantic feelings during a high-stakes trip.",
    "summary_short": "Poppy is a free-spirited travel writer living in New York, while Alex is a structured, quiet teacher who prefers the comfort of his small hometown. Despite their vastly different personalities, they formed a deep bond in college and spent one week together every summer taking an annual vacation. However, a ill-fated trip two years ago caused a major rift in their friendship, leading to radio silence. Realizing she is unhappy without him, Poppy convinces Alex to take one final trip to attend a family wedding, giving them one last chance to confront their past and figure out if they belong together.",
    "summary_long": "Poppy Wright and Alex Nilsen are complete opposites who met in college and unexpectedly became best friends during a long car ride back to their shared Ohio hometown. Establishing a tradition, they spent one week every summer taking budget vacations together across the globe, gradually developing deep but unexpressed feelings for one another. Their decade-long routine abruptly ended two years ago after a disastrous trip to Tuscany, where a near-kiss and a sudden romantic complication created an awkward distance between them. Feeling stuck and unfulfilled in her personal and professional life, Poppy reaches out to Alex to invite him on a trip to Barcelona for his brother's wedding, hoping to repair their bond. As they navigate their current vacation, flashbacks reveal the history of their previous trips, highlighting their unspoken longing, past relationships, and the miscommunications that kept them apart. The lingering tension eventually reaches a breaking point during the trip, forcing both of them to lay their true feelings on the table. However, their contrasting lifestyles—Poppy's fear of settling down and Alex's desire for stability—threaten to tear them apart once again. Realizing that fleeing from vulnerability is holding her back, Poppy takes a leap of faith to prove to Alex that he is her true home, leading the pair to finally commit to a shared future together.",
